^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-03-27 09:00] observe — prior approach assumed npm packages as primary distribution. User decided overnight that submodule model better preserves repository independence and engagement/exchange semantics.
 >>[2026-03-27 09:01] decide — workbench mounts at .spw/_workbench. The _ prefix signals infrastructure-not-content. Site's .spw/ surfaces are its own canon; workbench provides parser, runtime, LSP, CLI, and spec library underneath.
 >>[2026-03-27 09:02] decide — mount.spw is the engagement contract: it declares which workbench version the site tracks, which spec subsystems it engages with, and how resolution paths flow from site content through the engine.
 >>[2026-03-27 09:03] taste — this model is more honest than npm publish for early ecosystem: the relationship between repos is visible (git submodule), versionable (pin to commit), and reversible (remove submodule). npm can come later as a convenience layer once the protocol stabilizes.
 >>[2026-03-27 09:04] observe — independent consumers may already contain code and local conventions; each needs its own .spw authority rather than a copied workbench identity.
 >>[2026-03-27 09:05] decide — engagement is selective: a site doesn't adopt all 11 spec subsystems at once. mount.spw lists which subsystems are active. Exchange is contributory: a site can register new dialects or conventions that flow back through the submodule relationship.
 >>[2026-03-27 13:20] decide — treat this branch as the ecological anchor. Once commits 1-3 land, CLI init, CLI resolution, editor detection, health checks, docs, and governance mapping can proceed in parallel because they all share the same `_workbench` boundary.
 >>[2026-03-27 13:21] taste — ecological invigoration is not "more packages"; it is more independent sites entering the field with a clear mount contract, selective engagement, and a reversible relationship to the workbench.
 >>[2026-03-28 17:29] revise — the plan cache was stale after the site-install artifact, submodule convention, release-track truth, and portable site-init/doctor surfaces landed on main. The branch is no longer at commit 1, and install tooling already exists in CLI surfaces.
 >>[2026-03-28 17:29] observe — the remaining gap is shared mount resolution. `.spw/mount.spw` exists as seeded site metadata, but runtime and LSP still assume workbench-root defaults rather than deriving spec/CLI/LSP paths from the mounted `_workbench` contract.
 >>[2026-03-28 17:29] decide — treat commits 3 and 4 as one working arc: formalize mount.spw with tracked version + resolution paths, then export a runtime resolver that LSP and doctor can consume while keeping `.spw/_workbench` out of site-authored workspace scans.
 >>[2026-07-20 14:31] observe — mounted resolution landed in 45c6b7f3, but the plan still reported commit 3 as next and did not describe the repository-local model review that motivates mounting the workbench in developing consumers.
 >>[2026-07-20 14:32] decide — a repo-local model reads consumer-owned `.spw/` as authority, consults `.spw/_workbench` for protocols and instruments, and writes review artifacts back to consumer-owned surfaces with the mounted workbench revision recorded.
 >>[2026-07-20 14:33] decide — exchange is human-gated: consumers may contribute distilled claims, generated fixtures, or protocol improvements upstream, but the workbench does not automatically ingest consumer canon or review output.
 >>[2026-07-20 14:34] revise — use generated identity-free consumer fixtures so portability evidence never depends on a specific repository, domain, or predicted deployment shape.
 >>[2026-07-20 15:12] revise — add CLI observability as the next execution arc: root discovery, doctor, capability snapshots, and review orchestration must precede editor feature audits.
 >>[2026-08-24 10:14] observe — a scalar release number cannot tell a mounted consumer whether its language edition, syntax profile, AST/product schemas, runtime protocol, CLI envelope, and editor projection are mutually compatible.
 >>[2026-08-24 10:15] decide — mount, capabilities, and doctor disclose a compatibility vector with both revisions and per-capability status; `v0.4` remains a possible language gate, not a claim that all dimensions moved together.
 >>[2026-08-24 10:16] decide — resolved [review-entrypoint]: the mounted review skill owns authority/provenance procedure while CLI roots, doctor, capabilities, and probes remain composable instruments; no monolithic command is required.
 >>[2026-08-24 10:17] decide — resolved [review-retention]: generated caches are ephemeral, explicit consumer claims are durable by local policy, and upstream exchange is always a deliberate human-gated distillation.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:26] revise — Reconciled the 26 planned commits against history: seven landed hashes recorded in done, four concrete commits remain (spw capabilities, mount vector fields, doctor comparison, fixtures); three open questions sharpened to one-sentence decisions.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:26] observe — No spw capabilities command exists in packages/spw-cli/src; doctor reports pin drift against checkout head but has no compatibility vector; the init template scaffolds neither workspace paths nor tsconfig paths.
 >>[2026-10-12 15:29] revise — Commits named per the convention in 90c58bbc: 24 landed, 4 planned, 1 dropped.
}

